    <!-- https://www.web3d.org/documents/specifications/19774/V2.0/index.html -->
    <!-- Basic Pose 0 0 0 at floor between feet, default I pose (relaxed attention) model gaze +Z, +x to model left, +y up, right-hand rule. -->
    <!-- Jin loa4 v2 1:1 Only Landmarks https://www.web3d.org/documents/specifications/19774/V2.0/Architecture/concepts.html#BasicSetJointHierarchy4 with v2 Site surface feature point landmarks https://www.web3d.org/documents/specifications/19774/V2.0/Architecture/FeaturePoints.html The first part of this x3d xml user code listing includes definitions for the collection of Shapes that will be used to show the Joint center landmarks, with connecting lines to show the skeleton Joint hierarchy, and the surface feature Site landmarks with lines showing the Joints which control their basic motions. The skeleton structure user code is then. <HAnimHumanoid <HAnimJoint DEF='Joe_humanoid_root' name='humanoid_root' containerField='skeleton' center='0 0.826 -0.016'> <HAnimSegment DEF='Joe_sacrum' name='sacrum'> <Shape USE='JointMarker'/> <HAnimSite DEF='Joe_l_psis_pt' name='l_psis' translation='0.05 0.84 -0.11'> <Transform USE='l_psis_pt_SiteShape'/> </HAnimSite> </HAnimSegment> ... entire skeleton hierarchy ... </HAnimJoint> skin <Shape> geometry </Shape> </HAnimHumanoid Please Run the example. It starts with Kick2. Select any other Action from the menu. Animations for Pitch1, Yaw1, and Roll1 show basic operation by animation of each Joint of the skeleton and related Site surface feature landmarks. A colored sphere marker identifies a Site object. A line connects each Site to its parent Joint which controls its basic motion. The Pitch2, Yaw2, Roll2, Jump1, and Jump2 were connected from existing x3d HAnim archived example animations. All these need some work to show full loa4 articulation and the advantages of this standard skeleton hierarchy. Contents as follows: SceneViewpoints - set of scene viewpoint locations relative to the model 0 0 0 HAnimLandmarks - set of markers used to show landmarks of the model: Joint Shape Joint connections Site Shape Site Connections AnimationSelectMenu - hud selection plus a stationary rendering of DEFed assets. JointLandmarksAndJointConnections - DEF user code for Joint center location markers and skeleton connection hierarchy. SurfaceAndSiteDefinitions - DEF user code for the various Shape nodes for surface geometry and Site location markers and Site connections. Basic Default I pose All Joints = 0 0 1 0 Pose T | Pose A |Modify this set to experiment Pose H | Pitch1 Animation_loa4 Example x-axis rotations Pitch2 Animation_loa4 Example x-axis rotations Yaw1 Animation_loa4 Example y-axis rotations Yaw2 Animation_loa4 Example y-axis rotations Roll1 Animation_loa4 Example z-axis rotations Roll2 Animation_loa4 Example z-axis rotations Walk Animation_loa4 Example Walk animation Run Animation_loa4 Example Run animnation Jump Animation_loa4 Example Jump animation Kick1 Animation_loa4 Example Kick animation Kick2 Animation_loa4 Example Kick animation STOP Stop Animation - choose another Animation to start TimerControls Selection of timer for animation -->
    <!-- Joint x=Pitch1 y=Yaw1 z=Roll1 rotation timing 0.02 - 0.08 root translation 0.08 - 0.1 root rotation 0.2 - 0.3 sacro 0.25 - 0.75 eyeball 0.6 - 0.65 hip 0.65 0.70 knee 0.70 - 0.74 talocrural talocalcaneonavicular (1 2 3) calcaneocuboid (4 5) transversetarsal (4 5) cuneonavicular (1 2 3) tarsometatarsal (1 2 3 4 5) metatarsophalangeal (1 2 3 4 5) tarsal_interphalangeal (1) tarsal_proximal_interphalangeal (2 3 4 5) tarsal_distal_interphalangeal (2 3 4 5) 0.3 - 0.5 vl5 0.6 0.6375 vl2 0.6375 - 0.6875 vt10 0.6875 - 0.725 vt9 0.725 - 0.7875 vt5 0.7875 - 0.825 vt1 0.825 - 0.8625 vc7 0.8625 - 0.9 vc2 0.9 - 0.9985 skullbase 0.9 - 0.915 sterno 0.915 - 0.93 acrom 0.93 - 0.945 shoulder 0.945 - 0.96 elbow 0.96 - 0.98 radio 0.98 0.985 angeal_1 -->
